ill assume the old design:\n   - :434 heading \"runtime-neutral, reuse first\"\n   - :493 \"reusing one (E), which the phase 1 trial prices\"\n   - :617 cost row E \"trial review / a trial MR / ~5 trial\"\n   - :301-302 \"E ... is B's transport\"\n4. consider \u00b7 :605 \"Claude Code also throttles repeats\". It now applies only to Claude askers.\n5. consider \u00b7 :586-587 \"bills per API key, not under a runtime's subscription\". This is too broad given the local and albert providers in \u00a7 2.\n6. consider \u00b7 :545-548 retirement. When idh-wake's inbox is not empty at shutdown, it is kept with no card pointing to it. The no-ACK fallback covers this, and one clause would say so.\n7. consider \u00b7 :442-444 card fields `runtime` (now always Pi) and :424 \"live guichet\" are small two-path leftovers.\n\nChecked and consistent: no passage outside \u00a7 2 facts and the historical Review / follow-up lines still describes two paths, a one-shot run or claude --bg as host, and no tender names a model. The idh-wake.ts idle delivery claim (:111-113) matches the code. Today's pi --list-models gives the same provider counts (anthropic 17, openai 45, mistral 39, huggingface 81, padme-*, albert). `--mode rpc`, `--name` and `--session-id` are in pi --help. Detached delivery is marked \"Not yet observed\" (:117-120) and phase 1(a) tests it. The \u00a7 Protocol and path cross-references are retargeted correctly.\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 2m09s\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=1 tokens=na cost~=$na\nseat: consistency \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=sonnet \u00b7 model=anthropic/sonnet \u00b7 status: ran\nseat: piclaims \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=self \u00b7 model=anthropic/claude-opus-5-5 \u00b7 status: ran\nraw-output: seat=consistency \u00b7 door=claude-code \u00b7 model=sonnet \u00b7 raw_id=20261112T121312Z-101224\n"}

